      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Anubiasbarterivar.barteri(101A)/4551",
      "html": "<ul><li>Type: Rhizomatous</li><li>Origin: Africa</li><li>Growth rate: Slow</li><li>Height: 20-30+ cm (average height after two months in the tank)</li><li>Light demand: Low</li><li>CO2: Low</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Anubiasbarterivar.barteri(101A)/4551",
      "html": "<p>Anubias barteri var. barteri from West Africa is an undemanding plant. It grows somewhat larger than Anubias barteri var. nana but is grown in the same conditions. It is 25-45 cm tall and the creeping rhizome is 10-15 cm or more. Anubias barteri varies considerably in terms of size and leaf shape.</p><p>Like other Anubias species, it is best planted in a shady spot to minimize algae growth on the leaves. If planted on the bottom, the rhizome must not be covered because it tends to rot.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "tropica",
      "sourceUrl": "https://tropica.com/en/plants/plantdetails/Anubiasbarterivar.barteri(101A)/4551",
      "html": "<p>It is also suitable for terrariums and paludariums. Herbivorous fish do not eat the very tough and robust leaves.</p>"
    }
  ],
